# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Zen Shell — Monitor Watcher Configuration (v2)
# Path: ~/.config/hypr/zen-monitor-watcher.env
#
# Sourced by ~/.local/bin/zen-monitor-watcher.sh at startup.
# Uncomment and edit any line to override the default.
# Run `systemctl --user restart zen-monitor-watcher` after editing.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The internal display's connector name. Default is correct for most ROG
# laptops. For desktop-only setups, this still matters because the rescue
# fallback uses it. If you have no internal display, leave it as-is —
# the rescue is a no-op when the named connector isn't present.
# ZEN_MONITOR_INTERNAL=eDP-1

# Mode string used by the rescue fallback if it has to force-enable the
# internal display because no profile is loaded. Format matches `hyprctl
# keyword monitor`'s arg: "RESOLUTION,POSITION,SCALE"
# ZEN_MONITOR_INTERNAL_MODE=preferred,auto,1

# Set to 1 for "full dock mode" — the watcher will force-disable the internal
# whenever an external is connected (overriding any profile that might leave
# it on). Default 0 = use whatever the saved profile says.
# ZEN_MONITOR_DISABLE_INTERNAL_ON_EXTERNAL=0

# Where the watcher writes its log (truncated on each restart).
# ZEN_MONITOR_LOG=/tmp/zen-monitor-watcher.log

# Debounce in milliseconds after a socket2 event before re-querying state.
# Higher values let Hyprland fully settle but delay the response.
# ZEN_MONITOR_DEBOUNCE_MS=200

# ── v2 PROFILE SYSTEM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where saved per-topology profiles live. Each topology (unique combo of
# connected outputs) gets one .conf file here. Profiles are auto-saved
# AUTOSAVE_SEC seconds after a topology change settles, OR immediately
# via `zen-monitor-profile save`.
# ZEN_MONITOR_PROFILES_DIR=$HOME/.config/hypr/monitor-profiles

# How long to wait (in seconds) after the last monitor event before
# auto-saving the current state. Lower = catches manual edits faster
# but might save mid-adjustment. 5s is a good balance.
# ZEN_MONITOR_AUTOSAVE_SEC=5
